      "text": "To find the range of the set of numbers, we first need to answer some questions:\n\n1. How many numbers does the set of numbers have?\n2. What are the other two numbers in the set if we know one of them is 1?\n\nAs the mean is 4 and the median is 4 (the middle number in the set when ordered), this tells us that the other two numbers have the same mean as the first (1) and the same median as the others in the set: 4. Since there are two numbers in the set, they must sum to 8. If one is 4, the other must be 4.\n\nGiven the information above, we can now that the set of numbers has three elements (including the number 1), which are 1, 4, and 4. The range of the set denotes the difference between the largest and smallest input values in a set of numbers. In any set of numbers, the range is calculated as follows:\n\n[list]\n[*] {largest value} - {smallest value}\n[/list]\nIn the case of our numbers, the largest value is 4 and the smallest is 1. Therefore, the range of our set is 4 - 1 = 3.\n\nThe final answer is 3.\nTherefore, the range of the set of numbers is \\boxed{3}.",
